{"title":"Coral Pharmacy","sub":"Four warehouses into one?","type":"Cost & operations","industry":"Retail pharmacy","geo":"Australia","diff":2,"fmt":"Interviewer-led","time":"25-30 min","skills":"Network design · risk pooling · trade-offs","prompt":"Coral runs 600 pharmacies across eastern Australia, supplied from four regional warehouses. The supply chain director proposes closing three and serving every store from one large warehouse near Sydney. The CFO asks whether it would save money without hurting service.","clarify":[{"q":"Stock?","a":"Each warehouse holds safety stock to cover unexpected demand: $20M in total across the four."},{"q":"Holding cost?","a":"About 25% of stock value a year (capital, storage, expiry, insurance)."},{"q":"Fixed costs?","a":"Each warehouse costs about $1.5M a year to run, beyond the work of handling goods."},{"q":"Transport?","a":"Longer journeys from one site would add about $3M a year. About 15% of stores are more than 12 hours' drive from Sydney."}],"structure":{"root":"Should Coral consolidate to one warehouse?","branches":[{"head":"Inventory","items":["Safety stock needed in one place vs four"]},{"head":"Fixed costs","items":["Three warehouses closed"]},{"head":"Transport","items":["Longer distances"]},{"head":"Service","items":["Next-day delivery for distant stores"]}]},"hypothesis":"Pooling stock in one place needs less safety stock, because highs in one region offset lows in another. That saving, plus fewer sites, might outweigh extra transport, but distant stores could suffer.","questions":[{"q":"How much safety stock would one warehouse need?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>A common rule of thumb (the square-root law): if demand in each region is similar and independent, safety stock falls with the square root of the number of sites. Four sites into one: $20M ÷ √4 = <b>$10M</b>.</p> <p>Saving: $10M × 25% = <b>$2.5M a year</b>.</p>","note":"Demand in different regions partly cancels out when pooled."},{"q":"What is the net saving?","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"373.551719pt\" height=\"193.048pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 373.551719 193.048\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\"><defs><style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: butt}</style></defs><g id=\"figure_1\"><g id=\"patch_1\"><path d=\"M 0 193.048 L 373.551719 193.048 L 373.551719 0 L 0 0 L 0 193.048 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"axes_1\"><g id=\"patch_2\"><path d=\"M 20.391719 159.456 L 366.351719 159.456 L 366.351719 9.768 L 20.391719 9.768 L 20.391719 159.456 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"><g id=\"xtick_1\"><g id=\"line2d_1\"><defs><path id=\"mff7d576334\" d=\"M 0 0 L 0 3.5 \" style=\"stroke: #555555; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></defs><g><use xlink:href=\"#mff7d576334\" x=\"62.326264\" y=\"159.456\" style=\"fill: #555555; stroke: #555555; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_1\"><g style=\"fill: #555555\" transform=\"translate(44.645014 174.184) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-17\" d=\"M 1158 4749 Q 1235 4749 1235 4666 L 1235 109 Q 1235 45 1209 22 Q 1184 0 1120 0 L 717 0 Q 659 0 640 19 Q 621 38 621 90 L 621 4659 Q 621 4749 698 4749 L 1158 4749 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-5c\" d=\"M 582 0 Q 493 0 493 83 L 493 3309 Q 493 3392 563 3392 L 947 3392 Q 1018 3392 1018 3322 L 1018 2950 Q 1018 2918 1030 2912 Q 1043 2906 1075 2931 Q 1286 3098 1468 3216 Q 1651 3334 1843 3395 Q 2035 3456 2253 3456 Q 2752 3456 3017 3187 Q 3283 2918 3283 2490 L 3283 102 Q 3283 0 3187 0 L 2829 0 Q 2784 0 2765 22 Q 2746 45 2746 83 L 2746 2368 Q 2746 2682 2586 2858 Q 2426 3034 2080 3034 Q 1894 3034 1731 2973 Q 1568 2912 1401 2800 Q 1235 2688 1030 2515 L 1030 96 Q 1030 0 934 0 L 582 0 L 582 0 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-72\" d=\"M 3251 3392 Q 3296 3392 3315 3363 Q 3334 3334 3315 3296 L 2016 96 Q 1984 0 1869 0 L 1638 0 Q 1517 0 14